--- !u!114 &6009446447907924950
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 5326867582145011389}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 517c9c51fb9658740ab6a0ac4749be52, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Client1Greeting:
  - Salutations!
  - I, the legendary General Buzzard, require your assistance in getting myself a
    brand new...
  - Special "honey"...
  - As I am preparing for my upcoming...
  - Epic battle.
  Client1Request:
  - But, as you may predict, I require more than just a plain ol' gun.
  - It has to be something greater!
  - Something that could turn the tides of war!
  - I desire a gun that will make all my enemies shiver!
  - It has to be loud, fast and full of bullets!
  - And none of that girly stuff.
  - Can you create something like that? Or am I wasting my breath?
  Client1ResponseGood:
  - Excellent! This weapon of mass destruction is worth all my money!
  - Great job cadet!
  Client1ResponseAverage:
  - Oh... It's just a plain old gun...
  - But I guess this will do.
  Client1ResponseBad:
  - Great heavens, you call this a weapon?!
  - Are you trying to insult me?!
  Client2Greeting:
  - Hello Mr. Bee Bee's.
  - I am a representative of the B.E.Z. Company.
  - Time is money, so let's cut straight to the chase.
  Client2Request:
  - We are preparing to cut down a huge chunk of forest.
  - We need something that will minimize the costs and maximize the efficiency.
  - I'm not talking about a simple chainsaw nor any other conventional equipment...
  - The more blades it has, the better, as long as the timber remains in sellable
    condition.
  - Oh, and make sure it's eco-friendly or whatever. Shareholders love that!
  Client2ResponseGood:
  - My, my... You are better than I thought.
  - Please doing business with you.
  Client2ResponseAverage:
  - As I said before, time is money.
  - This thing will barely save my company any time and any money.
  Client2ResponseBad:
  - Tsk... I'd be better off punching the trees with my bare hands.
  - You've just lost a deal of a lifetime.
  Client3Greeting:
  - Howdy, friend!
  - I've heard a lot of good things about this store of yours...
  - So I've decided to *shoot my shot*.
  Client3Request:
  - The hunting tournament is growing near and while I love the shooting part...
  - Cooking the meat is just so boring! That's just a damn chore.
  - When I see prey in the distance, I want to kill it and eat it right then and
    there!
  - Any chance you can make me a rifle with a built-in BBQ?
  Client3ResponseGood:
  - You son of a gun, this is exactly what I was looking for!
  - I won't have to waste my time grilling my meat ever again.
  Client3ResponseAverage:
  - Darn... It's... Alright I suppose.
  - Just hope it doesn't let me down during the hunt.
  Client3ResponseBad:
  - Which part of "I HATE COOKING" did you not understand?!
  - You're an amateur, dang nabbit!
  Client4Greeting:
  - Hello darling, aren't you something sweet?
  - Look, I'm not really familiar with places like this.
  - But I heard you could help me with a little problem of mine...
  Client4Request:
  - You see... I've met this wonderful guy. Rich, I might add!
  - Until one day, I've caught a glimpse of his bank account, only to find out that
    he lost almost all of his money!
  - How cruel of him to lie to me like that!
  - I want to teach him a lesson, with a gun as glamorous and elegant as me.
  - Would you help this damsel in distress, darling?
  Client4ResponseGood:
  - That's marvelous!
  - This should teach him how to treat a lady.
  Client4ResponseAverage:
  - I thought you were better than this...
  - At least it's not my credit card.
  Client4ResponseBad:
  - Ugh, this is quite dreadful.
  - I wouldn't dream of being seen with something so ugly.
  Client5Greeting:
  - Let's make this clear. You're still alive, because I want you alive.
  - One wrong move and you'll end up like one of my many targets.
  Client5Request:
  - I'm not looking for a gun. I've got plenty of those.
  - I'm looking for... The perfect tool.
  - Something slow, something percise and something quiet.
  - Something that won't get me killed working under cover of night.
  - All in a one, reliable package.
  - Do not mess this up.
  Client5ResponseGood:
  - Yes... Perfect...
  - Let's hope we'll never have to meet again.
  - Or it won't end too well for you.
  Client5ResponseAverage:
  - I'm a professional, and professionals have standards.
  - This thing does not meet them.
  Client5ResponseBad:
  - ...
  - Once I'm done with my target, you're next on my list.
  Client6Greeting:
  - Um... hi. I'm just...
  - I'm just looking I guess.
  - Do you sell, uh... guns?
  Client6Request:
  - Well... I thought maybe this place would be... the last stop.
  - Could you avoid adding sharp edges? Or... I dunno...
  - Use some cheap parts, please. I don't want to be a bother more than I already
    am.
  - Damn it... I'm such a coward. If only I could aim the gun in another direction...
  - ...Sorry, I know that sounds weird.
  Client6ResponseGood:
  - Wow.. that's... just what I was looking for.
  - Thank you for ending my misery... I won't forget that.
  Client6ResponseAverage:
  - Um... Are you sure this will work?
  - I... I guess I'll give it a shot.
  Client6ResponseBad:
  - That's... not what I was expecting. It must be alll my fault.
  - I'm terrible at whatever I do... I can't even end it correctly.
  Client7Greeting:
  - 'Pryvit... mmmph... '
  - Rrmmh... weapon... order... phhm...
  Client7Request:
  - Mfff... Kersk... rrrgh... nuclear... reactor...
  - Hhmmp... light... hmpff... for... darkness... rhhmm...
  - Mutants... mffpf... kaboom... mmhr... Ha!
  - Mfff... make... automatic...
  Client7ResponseGood:
  - Djakuju... hmpp...!
  - Fantastic... rrhrff... gun... ffrmp...
  Client7ResponseAverage:
  - Seen... better... tchhp...
  - Hmmpf... survive... ffrt... maybe...
  Client7ResponseBad:
  - Rrrghh... insult... weapon...? Pfah!
  - Hmpff... mmgh... useless...!
